WEBVTT

00:03:58.796 --> 00:04:01.196
I also just want to end
with maybe three concepts

00:04:01.236 --> 00:04:04.516
that are really big in the book
and maybe a little bit of a foundation

00:04:04.516 --> 00:04:06.516
for what we're going to talk about today.

00:04:06.516 --> 00:04:09.636
The book is about women of color
and finding power, forging power.

00:04:09.676 --> 00:04:12.036
And one of the biggest ideas in the book

00:04:12.076 --> 00:04:14.836
is that corporate America
is not a meritocracy

00:04:14.836 --> 00:04:16.916
and that we need to talk about that,

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.556
at least in the American context.

00:04:18.556 --> 00:04:21.156
Until about two years ago,
until George Floyd's murder,

00:04:21.196 --> 00:04:23.236
we weren't able to talk
about race at work.

00:04:23.236 --> 00:04:25.196
It wasn't something that was acknowledged

00:04:25.236 --> 00:04:27.436
or I feel like we had
permission to talk about.

00:04:27.476 --> 00:04:30.436
And there definitely wasn't
willingness or openness to the idea